DRAFT — BUYER DETAILS, DELIVERY DETAILS, AND SIGNATURES REQUIRED

This Exclusive Proprietary Commercial Source Code Licence Agreement (the “Agreement”) is entered into as of [EFFECTIVE DATE] (the “Effective Date”) by and between:

Licensor: PANAMULLA ARACHCHIGE SADARES DENUWAN, an individual resident of Sri Lanka, of [LICENSOR ADDRESS] (“Licensor”); and

Licensee: [BUYER FULL LEGAL NAME], [an individual / a company incorporated under the laws of JURISDICTION with registration number NUMBER], of [BUYER ADDRESS] (“Licensee”).

Licensor and Licensee are each a “Party” and together the “Parties”. This Agreement is not effective until the buyer details, delivery details, and Effective Date are completed and both Parties have signed it.

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 “Licensed Product” means the Deriv-specific trading-bot source-code snapshot identified by the delivery commit hash or archive checksum in Schedule 1, together with the documentation, tests, and other items expressly marked “Included” in Schedule 1. It excludes Reserved Technology, Excluded Assets, Third-Party Materials, and later versions unless expressly added by a signed amendment.

1.2 “Deriv-Specific Field” means software whose primary purpose is to connect to Deriv APIs and provide the functionality of the Licensed Product. It does not include generic trading, simulation, risk, networking, dashboard, or development technology used outside a Deriv-specific product.

1.3 “Reserved Technology” means Licensor’s generic simulator framework, generic risk-engine components, generic WebSocket and reconnection utilities, generic dashboard utilities, pre-existing code, development tools, methods, know-how, and reusable libraries, including improvements that are not specific to the Licensed Product.

1.4 “Third-Party Materials” means software, APIs, data, trademarks, documentation, and other materials owned or controlled by third parties, including Rust crates and Deriv services or content.

1.5 “Excluded Assets” means all items listed in Schedule 2.

1.6 “Material Defect” means a reproducible failure of the delivered Licensed Product, as delivered and used in the documented supported environment, to materially conform to an express acceptance criterion in Schedule 1. A missing future feature, trading outcome, provider change, unsupported environment, or item disclosed in the known-limitations document is not a Material Defect.

