11.4 LICENSOR DOES NOT WARRANT DERIV OR ANY OTHER THIRD-PARTY API, DATA, AUTHENTICATION METHOD, ENDPOINT, RATE LIMIT, CONTRACT, MARKET, OR SERVICE. LICENSEE ASSUMES ALL TRADING, DEPLOYMENT, SECURITY, DATA, PROVIDER, AND COMPLIANCE RISK.

12. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

12.1 TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, NEITHER PARTY IS LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, PUNITIVE, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS, LOST REVENUE, LOST DATA, LOST BUSINESS, TRADING LOSSES, OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, ARISING FROM OR RELATED TO THIS AGREEMENT, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY.

12.2 TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, LICENSOR’S TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY ARISING FROM OR RELATED TO THIS AGREEMENT WILL NOT EXCEED THE LICENCE FEE ACTUALLY RECEIVED BY LICENSOR.

12.3 Nothing in this Agreement excludes or limits liability to the extent it cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, including liability for fraud or intentional misconduct. The cap does not limit Licensee’s payment obligations, breach of source-code restrictions, unauthorized sublicensing or transfer, or infringement of Licensor’s intellectual-property rights. The express ownership warranty remains subject to the remedy in Section 10.2 to the extent permitted by law.

13. TERM AND TERMINATION

13.1 This Agreement begins on the Effective Date and, subject to full payment, the licence is perpetual unless terminated under this Section.

13.2 Either Party may terminate for a material breach not cured within thirty (30) days after detailed written notice. A breach involving unauthorized source disclosure, sublicensing, transfer, or deliberate infringement that is incapable of cure may be terminated immediately to the extent permitted by law.

13.3 On termination for Licensee breach, Licensee must stop using the Licensed Product and permanently delete all copies, except one archival copy retained only if required by law and not used. Accrued payment, confidentiality, ownership, restrictions, disclaimers, liability, dispute, and other provisions intended by nature to survive will survive.

14. DISPUTE RESOLUTION, GOVERNING LAW, AND LANGUAGE

14.1 Before commencing court proceedings, the Parties will attempt in good faith for thirty (30) days after written dispute notice to resolve the dispute through authorized representatives. Either Party may seek urgent interim or injunctive relief without waiting where necessary to protect confidential information or intellectual-property rights.

14.2 This Agreement is governed by the laws of Sri Lanka, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Subject to Section 14.1, the courts located in Colombo, Sri Lanka have exclusive jurisdiction, and each Party submits to those courts.

14.3 This Agreement is written in English. Any translation is for convenience only; the English version controls to the extent of inconsistency.

